<title>USA: Conservative values set at Armstrong Shaw-Barron's.</title>
<headline>Conservative values set at Armstrong Shaw-Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The investment firm that once handled the investments of President Ronald Reagan no longer has the former president's account, but it continues to adhere to a conservative investment of undervalued stocks.</p>
<p>Armstrong Shaw Associates, based in Stamford, Conn., said in an interview with the financial weekly Barron's that the firm &quot;invests in securities only when cash-flow or asset-value analysis determines they are selling at substantial discounts to their intrinsic values.&quot;  </p>
<p>Stocks picked by the firm in the interview as good invesments on this basis include Alleghany Corp, Hilton Hotels Corp, Comcast Corp, Armco Inc, Chase Manhattan Corp, Travelers Group Inc, Fannie Mae, and Chris-Craft Industries Inc.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk 212.859.1610</p>
